#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046647} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563766} :activity/id #uuid "2fc03e67-f529-57d4-bd70-e937a60ca493" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048299 :topic/id #uuid "92705545-a0a9-5765-ace5-b1ebda874c1c" :topic/math-academy-id 633} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563766 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078737 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a03f1c4-85f0-544a-98ce-eb511fe07eaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075299} {:answer/id #uuid "0a671052-347b-512f-9f82-a17f56d9b608" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075300} {:answer/id #uuid "39c25198-703a-5df7-aa3a-a52a10dde17f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075301} {:answer/id #uuid "4ee76099-e24e-58a0-bb4f-7e88b011ff6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075302} {:answer/id #uuid "5fa3c182-4108-54cf-ac41-2c7b914e0c29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075303}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186075301} :answer-field/id #uuid "daf6a544-6cab-5dae-af57-5b6a03128e40" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075298}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a297f665-c83d-57c5-a5b3-4e4cdbf2c7d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-14581" :question/problem "![](images/d0/d04a8e993da8e90ca75f5f7541317d26a6a9c8f9b76cdb9c95511080035177c5.png)\n\nFind the cosine of $∠Y.$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Recall the definition of cosine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡Y=\\frac{\\text{adjacent}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}=\\frac{XY}{YZ}=\\frac{XY}{5}\n$$\n\nHere, we need to determine the missing side $XY.$ The trick is to use the Pythagorean Theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{Y{Z}^{2}-X{Z}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}-(\\sqrt{7})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25-7} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{18} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡Y & =\\frac{XY}{5}=\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "19daaae6-6d2a-56f2-a06f-7650bdc33cd8" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563774}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563774 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563724 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2561f127-b662-5797-b919-80264e333b26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563030} {:answer/id #uuid "35b1eb42-ba69-53f4-81c2-c8740d0d9806" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563067} {:answer/id #uuid "493e3c85-b25e-53b6-a08c-4fea9dba4c1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563106} {:answer/id #uuid "c48feefc-15c4-5bef-ac32-e7d9d07bb0ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563376} {:answer/id #uuid "d04f3cfc-1715-5df0-995f-34492b52003c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563402}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563067} :answer-field/id #uuid "f15bdbe8-d486-594d-b02d-d29460c4afc4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563637}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b2b55850-322e-5b17-9a94-b2696bd083f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-122050" :question/problem "In the right triangle $△JKL,$ $∠J$ is a right angle, $JL=8$ and $KL=12.$ Find $\\operatorname{tan}⁡K.$" :question/worked-solution "The following triangle illustrates the information given.\n\n![](images/cc/cc33327cc6d071cb6ec9ac0c10d58e57bc35f8d81b326731120cf04c18f58ec1.png)\n\nRecall the definition of tangent: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡K=\\frac{\\text{opposite}}{\\text{adjacent}}=\\frac{JL}{JK}=\\frac{8}{JK}\n$$\n\nHere, we need to determine the missing side $JK.$ The trick is to use the Pythagorean Theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}JK & =\\sqrt{K{L}^{2}-J{L}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{12}^{2}-{8}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{144-64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{80} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡K & =\\frac{8}{4\\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "311cff77-4b9d-5219-ae3d-48aca39552db" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563809}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563809 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563680 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24c3606f-796c-5b0b-8a50-19ba888da79b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563027} {:answer/id #uuid "9a5b3adb-f36e-546f-90c5-4151e04b2960" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{21}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563293} {:answer/id #uuid "b43265d8-cc49-526f-8e22-5651c777ca5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563342} {:answer/id #uuid "dcdc4442-a9d9-5305-bc8b-adc1a7389cb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563429} {:answer/id #uuid "f46bc196-b847-5053-8f6e-796c26a26b99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{24}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563492}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563492} :answer-field/id #uuid "518b1e5c-6389-594b-b333-90ba109eabdc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563565}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "44ffb250-1ebe-5832-a06b-038dd7ff73b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-122171" :question/problem "![](images/0b/0bff27a71fc8421d51e69a677260f60a1e421c09fe3969f70d4c07bf1ac58576.png)\n\nFind the tangent of $∠P.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall the definition of tangent: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡P=\\frac{\\text{opposite}}{\\text{adjacent}}=\\frac{QR}{PQ}=\\frac{QR}{3.5}\n$$\n\nHere, we need to determine the missing length $QR.$ The trick is to use the Pythagorean Theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}QR & =\\sqrt{P{R}^{2}-P{Q}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{12.5}^{2}-{3.5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{156.25-12.25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{144} \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡P & =\\frac{QR}{3.5} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{3.5} \\\\  & =\\frac{120}{35} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "e42c4ff4-4729-582c-9103-cb4c5fbad322"}] :activity/title "Calculating Trigonometric Ratios Using the Pythagorean Theorem" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562925}]}
